<title>BELGIUM: EU cuts monthly malt export refunds.</title>
<headline>EU cuts monthly malt export refunds.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee cut back monthly malt export refunds with effect from Friday December 20 because of the high level of applications for licences, an EU official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The committee set malt refund rates with effect from today (Friday),&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The rates were as follows -</p>
<p>			  Dec 20		  Previous</p>
<p>    wheat malt	8 Ecus per tonne    25.50 Ecus per tonne</p>
<p>    barley malt    15 Ecus per tonne    37.86 Ecus per tonne</p>
<p>    roasted malt   20 Ecus per tonne    43.84 Ecus per tonne</p>
<p>The Commisson reported that licence bookings had reached 1.8 million tonnes in the year and current application were at 400.000 tonnes. It said that malt export refunds might not need to be restored in the New Year, the official reported.</p>
</text>
